    "reason": "THE PERIOD WALL WITH NO AUTOMATON IN IT. This is the one recommendation of the attack document of 2026-09-09 ('Two unexplained numbers from today's kernel checks', section 4) that has not landed: its author names it as what they would seed first, 'the only one of the four that puts something new UNDER a wall', because it moves leftDiagonal_period_le into the same N-only arithmetic frame where leftDiagonal_onset_le now lives. That matters concretely rather than aesthetically. Both walls are now claims about the orbit of a single number under r -> 4r XOR (2r OR r); one script measures both, one induction could attack both, and the whole packed-row toolkit the board landed on 2026-09-10 and the four nodes above become available to the period wall, which currently has none of it. Why the equivalence holds. Backward is one line: leftDiagonal_periodicFrom_of_rowNat_agree_any at k = n-1 turns the congruence into a period p <= n = (n-1)+1 for diagonal n-1. Forward is the work, and it has a route that needs no maximum over onsets. For each j < n take the given period p_j <= j+1 and the power-of-two period 2^j from leftDiagonal_periodicFrom_pow; periodicFrom_gcd makes q_j = gcd(p_j, 2^j) a period, a power of two, and at most p_j <= n. periodicFrom_trans_period then moves every one of them onto the uniform onset 2^j <= 2^n that leftDiagonal_periodicFrom_pow already supplies, so no max is needed. Now take q = 2 ^ Nat.log 2 n, the largest power of two at most n: every q_j is a power of two at most n, hence divides q, so periodicFrom_mul puts all n diagonals on the single period q <= n. Finally leftDiagonal_eq_rowNat_testBit reads those n agreements off as the n low bits of rows T and T+q at T = 2^n + n, and Nat.eq_of_testBit_eq assembles the congruence. Measured: the arithmetic side holds for every n from 1 to 700, and the least power of two that works steps up at n = 1, 4, 9, 30, 401 -- which is exactly the known doubling depths 3, 8, 29, 400 shifted by one, an independent reproduction of NKS p. 871 and of crystal 57's staircase from this statement alone (explorer/tessera_ladder.mjs).",
